I fixed the last open row of #1072. On a detached HEAD, /pr create now says so instead of claiming you're not in a git repository. Build, test, clippy and fmt all pass, and it's committed as e02edb46.

What I changed
• New check: pr_create_branch_in(dir) in src/commands_git_pr.rs. When there's no current branch, it uses git rev-parse --git-dir to tell the two cases apart. That command succeeds in any repo, detached or unborn, and fails outside one. The /pr create call site now goes through this check.
• Detached HEAD: it prints error: HEAD is detached; check out a branch before /pr create (git switch -c <name>) and stops before any diff or gh call. I ran gh pr create (gh 2.102.0) on a detached HEAD in a temp repo first. It fails with "could not determine the current branch … not on any branch", so the advice doesn't contradict it.
• Outside a repo: the message is still exactly error: not in a git repository.

Tests, in the new src/commands_git_pr_create_tests.rs, all in temp repos:
• detached HEAD gets the detached message;
• not a repo gets the old message, checked against the full string;
• a normal branch passes through unchanged;
• a fresh git init with no commits passes through and isn't mistaken for detached.

To check the detached test can actually fail, I briefly made that case return the old message: only the detached test went red, and I restored the code in the same command.

Two repo checks caught my first draft:
• The git-chokepoint check rejected my test helper because it ran git directly. It now goes through run_git_in_dir, like the undo tests do.
• The orphan-module check needs the module name to match the file name, so I renamed it to mod commands_git_pr_create_tests.

Also done
• Added the detached-HEAD behaviour to the /pr create line in docs/src/usage/commands.md.
• git grep '#1072' finds only comments describing past fixes, including my new doc comment. None of them is a "tracked in" pointer, so they stay true once the ticket closes.
• I commented on #1072 with the sha and noted this is the /pr row from the 09:50Z ledger. I posted it before pushing, so the comment says the fix arrives with this session's push, and "Fixes #1072" will close the ticket then.
